  "worked_solution": "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=-4.5$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{2}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=5.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=3.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(5)=-4.5+3.5=-1.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x=-1.$",
